          "title": "Linear equations in 12 minutes",
          "meta": "12:10",
          "source": {
            "type": "lesson",
            "lessonId": "v1"
          },
          "content": {
            "kind": "video",
            "duration": "12:10",
            "notes": [
              {
                "at": "01:05",
                "text": "Slope-intercept form is y = mx + b: m is the slope, b is where the line meets the y-axis."
              },
              {
                "at": "05:40",
                "text": "To solve, undo operations in reverse order on both sides."
              },
              {
                "at": "09:12",
                "text": "A coefficient in front of x scales the slope, not the intercept."
              }
            ]
          },
          "fullTitle": "Linear equations in 12 minutes"
        },
        {
          "id": "v2",
          "kind": "video",
          "moduleId": "m1",
          "title": "Systems of equations",
          "meta": "14:32",
          "source": {
            "type": "lesson",
            "lessonId": "v2"
          },
          "content": {
            "kind": "video",
            "duration": "14:32",
            "notes": [
              {
                "at": "00:42",
                "text": "A system is two equations that share the same x and y. The solution is where the lines cross."
              },
              {
                "at": "03:15",
                "text": "Substitution: solve one equation for y, then plug it into the other."
              },
              {
                "at": "06:58",
                "text": "Elimination: scale and add the equations so one variable cancels."
              }
            ]
          },
          "fullTitle": "Systems of equations: substitution and elimination"
        },
        {
          "id": "v3",
          "kind": "video",
          "moduleId": "m1",
          "title": "Inequalities and word problems",
          "meta": "16:05",
